Candidate source-facing theorem:

theorem standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 < eta s) (hsmall : ∀ s, eta s ≤ 1) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u => V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let Q := fun s u => ‖u‖^2/2+rho s u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)
      let R := fun s => mu.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s => (R s).map (fun x => (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      IsProbabilityMeasure mu ∧
        ∀ s, IsProbabilityMeasure (R s) ∧
          ContDiff ℝ 2 (rho s) ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 (Q s) ∧
          gradient (rho s) 0=0 ∧ gradient (Q s) 0=0 ∧
          (∀ u v : E, 0 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ eta s*‖v‖^2) ∧
          (∀ u v : E, ‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (1+eta s)*‖v‖^2) ∧
          r s=(volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u => -Q s u) ∧
          IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧ MemLp id 2 (r s) ∧
          Integrable (fun u => ‖u‖^2) (r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E ∧
          MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧
          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤
            (eta s)^2*Module.finrank ℝ E

No supplied proximal selector/optimality, posterior probability, normalized
affine-law identity, curvature/gradient regularity, stationary point or moment.
All genuine source definitions appear literally. Actual map and normalized tilted
law must coincide by a real affine change of variables with finite positive
partition and correct Jacobian, not by comparing unnormalized potential formulas.
Finite Hilbert/Borel, dimension zero and arbitrary measurable S are disclosed
extensions; paper standing beta1/kappainv/eta<=1 retained.

Exact full-range proximal producer and existing GibbsPositionMoment are required
actual parents; no duplicate Banach selector, Gaussian moment or noncompact IBP.
This does not prove the first inequality of (4.6): Gaussian Talagrand+LSI remains
separate. No W2 distance, bias(4.2), Gaussian MGF(4.3), full Lemma4.2, higher
smoothing, joint posterior Markov kernel measurability, numerical proximal
implementation/cost, HMC/PBPS invariance/accuracy, warmness/initialization,
main theorem or actual-input expected-query-cost composition is admitted.
TV never transfers unbounded cost; this actual r/R are not the Gaussian gradient
output kernel, exact-gradient K, stochastic-exact-prox Khat or mean Kbar.
